+# STORY-094: Keyword Bids Batch Sync + Cache — Test Design
+
+## Scope
+
+Small story following the existing `@cache_first` pattern. Tests cover the new
+`@cache_first` decorator on `sp_list_keywords` and the `sync_cycle` keyword
+fetch addition.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria → Test Mapping
+
+| AC | Description | Test(s) |
+|----|-------------|---------|
+| AC-1 | `sync_cycle` fetches keywords and caches them under `"sp_list_keywords"` | `test_sync_cycle_fetches_and_caches_keywords` |
+| AC-2 | Cache hit returns without calling Amazon API | `test_cache_hit_returns_cached_keywords`, `test_no_outbound_http_on_cache_hit` |
+| AC-3 | Cache miss calls live API, caches result, second call is cache hit | `test_cache_miss_calls_live_api_and_caches` |
+| AC-4 | `ad_group_id`/`campaign_id` filters applied client-side from cache | `test_filter_by_ad_group_id_uses_cache_not_api`, `test_filter_by_campaign_id_uses_cache_not_api` |
+| AC-5 | Response includes `source` and `cache_age_seconds` | `test_response_metadata_fields` |
+| AC-6 | Zero outbound HTTP calls in all tests | All tests mock `ads_client`; `test_no_outbound_http_on_cache_hit` patches httpx |
+| AC-7 | ≥6 test cases covering all required scenarios | 8 tests total |
+
+## Test Cases
+
+### TC-1: `test_cache_hit_returns_cached_keywords` (AC-2)
+
+**Scenario:** In-memory TtlCache already has keyword data.
+
+**Setup:**
+- Pre-populate TtlCache with keyword list under operation `"sp_list_keywords"`
+- Mock `ads_client` — `list_sp_keywords` will raise if called
+
+**Assertions:**
+- `client.list_sp_keywords` NOT called
+- `result["source"]` is not `"live_api"` (i.e., from cache)
+- `result["cache_age_seconds"]` exists and is numeric
+
+**RED reason:** Current `sp_list_keywords` always calls `client.list_sp_keywords` regardless of cache state.
+
+---
+
+### TC-2: `test_cache_miss_calls_live_api_and_caches` (AC-3)
+
+**Scenario:** Cache empty → live API called → result cached → second call is cache hit.
+
+**Setup:**
+- Empty TtlCache
+- Mock `client.list_sp_keywords` returns keyword list
+
+**Assertions:**
+- First call: `client.list_sp_keywords` called exactly once with `(profile_id,)` only — no filter args
+- `result["source"] == "live_api"`
+- Second call: `client.list_sp_keywords` NOT called again (served from cache)
+
+**RED reason:** Current code never writes to cache so second call still hits the API.
+
+---
+
+### TC-3: `test_filter_by_ad_group_id_uses_cache_not_api` (AC-4)
+
+**Scenario:** Cache populated with keywords spanning two ad groups; filter requested.
+
+**Setup:**
+- Pre-populate cache with 6 keywords across `ag_000` (3 keywords) and `ag_001` (3 keywords)
+
+**Assertions:**
+- `client.list_sp_keywords` NOT called
+- Returned keywords all have `adGroupId == "ag_000"`
+- `total_count` equals the filtered subset count
+
+**RED reason:** Current code passes `ad_group_id` filter directly to API rather than filtering cached data.
+
+---
+
+### TC-4: `test_filter_by_campaign_id_uses_cache_not_api` (AC-4)
+
+**Scenario:** Cache populated; `campaign_id` filter applied client-side.
+
+**Setup:**
+- Pre-populate cache with keywords across `camp_000` and `camp_001`
+
+**Assertions:**
+- `client.list_sp_keywords` NOT called
+- Returned keywords all have `campaignId == "camp_000"`
+
+**RED reason:** Same as TC-3.
+
+---
+
+### TC-5: `test_sync_cycle_fetches_and_caches_keywords` (AC-1)
+
+**Scenario:** `sync_cycle` runs and includes keyword fetch for each profile.
+
+**Setup:**
+- Mock `api_cache` (AsyncMock) with `async_set`, `async_get`, `async_invalidate`
+- Mock `_fetch_sp_keywords` (or underlying `AdsApiClient.list_sp_keywords`) to return keywords
+- Mock `_get_access_token` to bypass LWA token fetch
+- Mock `write_entity` to bypass DB writes
+
+**Assertions:**
+- `api_cache.async_set` called with `operation="sp_list_keywords"`
+
+**RED reason:** `sync_cycle` does not currently include `_fetch_sp_keywords` in its fetch tasks.
+
+---
+
+### TC-6: `test_cache_key_uses_sp_list_keywords_operation` (AC-7 — cache key correctness)
+
+**Scenario:** After a cache miss + live fetch, the TtlCache contains data under the correct operation key.
+
+**Setup:**
+- Empty TtlCache instance
+- Mock `client.list_sp_keywords` returns keyword list
+
+**Assertions:**
+- After calling `sp_list_keywords(profile_id=PROFILE_ID)`, a direct `api_cache.get(...)` with `operation="sp_list_keywords"` returns `(True, <data>)`
+
+**RED reason:** Current code never writes to cache so the operation key is never populated.
+
+---
+
+### TC-7: `test_no_outbound_http_on_cache_hit` (AC-6)
+
+**Scenario:** Cache is warm; httpx is patched to raise on any network call.
+
+**Setup:**
+- Pre-populate TtlCache with keyword data
+- Patch `httpx.AsyncClient` to raise `RuntimeError("no outbound HTTP allowed")`
+
+**Assertions:**
+- `sp_list_keywords` completes without raising (no HTTP call was made)
+- Result contains keyword data from cache
+
+**RED reason:** Without `@cache_first`, the current code would reach `client.list_sp_keywords`, which internally uses httpx, triggering the assertion.
+
+---
+
+### TC-8: `test_response_metadata_fields` (AC-5)
+
+**Scenario:** Verify presence and correctness of `source` and `cache_age_seconds` in both cache-hit and cache-miss paths.
+
+**Cache-hit assertions:**
+- `result["cached"] is True`
+- `result["cache_age_seconds"] >= 0`
+- `result["source"]` in `("memory_cache", "db_cache")`
+
+**Cache-miss (live) assertions:**
+- `result["source"] == "live_api"`
+- `result["cache_age_seconds"] == 0.0`
+
+**RED reason:** Current code returns `{"source": "live_api", "staleness": "real-time"}` — no `cached` field, no `cache_age_seconds`.
+
+---
+
+## Edge Cases (not in minimal test set but noted)
+
+- **Empty keyword list**: sync_cycle should NOT cache empty results (poison prevention); @cache_first decorator also skips empty results.
+- **Multiple profiles isolated**: Cache keys are scoped to `(user_id, profile_id, operation)` — keywords from profile A are not visible when querying profile B.
+- **Pagination**: `offset`/`limit` are applied after client-side filtering by the decorator; the full list is always cached.
+
+## External API Isolation
+
+All tests mock `src.tools.sp_tools.ads_client`. The `@cache_first` decorator calls the wrapped function only on cache miss, and the wrapped function uses `ads_client` (module-level injectable). This means:
+
+- In tests: `ads_client` is replaced with an `AsyncMock`
+- The real `AdsApiClient` is never instantiated in tests
+- `test_no_outbound_http_on_cache_hit` provides a belt-and-suspenders network-level guard
+
+Zero outbound HTTP calls to `advertising-api.amazon.com` are possible in the test suite.
